<title>USA: GM says 23,340 workers idle, down slightly.</title>
<headline>GM says 23,340 workers idle, down slightly.</headline>
<dateline>WARREN, Mich. 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp said that as of 1100 EDT/1500 GMT Friday, 23,340 of its workers in the U.S. and Mexico were idle as a result of the strike by the Canadian Auto Workers union that ended earlier this week.</p>
<p>The figure is down from 23,801 idle GM workers late on Thursday.</p>
<p>Canadian Auto Workers ratified a tentative deal on a new contract on Tuesday and are returning to their jobs in stages.</p>
<p>GM said an update will be issued at 1600 EDT/2100 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Chicago Newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
